## 2. Multi-Query Attention (MQA)

### Comparison with Vanilla Transformer:
- **Vanilla Transformer**: Each head has separate Q, K, V matrices
- **MQA**: Single K, V shared across all heads, separate Q for each head
- **Benefits**: Reduced memory usage, faster inference, maintained quality
- **Memory Reduction**: ~50% reduction in KV cache size
- **Used in**: PaLM, Falcon models

### Code Example:
```python
# Vanilla Multi-Head Attention
class VanillaMultiHeadAttention(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, d_model, num_heads):
        self.num_heads = num_heads
        self.d_head = d_model // num_heads
        
        self.q_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)  # num_heads * d_head
        self.k_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)  # num_heads * d_head
        self.v_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)  # num_heads * d_head

# Multi-Query Attention
class MultiQueryAttention(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, d_model, num_heads):
        self.num_heads = num_heads
        self.d_head = d_model // num_heads
        
        self.q_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, d_model)  # num_heads * d_head
        self.k_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, self.d_head)  # Single head
        self.v_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, self.d_head)  # Single head
    
    def forward(self, x):
        B, L, D = x.shape
        
        Q = self.q_proj(x).view(B, L, self.num_heads, self.d_head)
        K = self.k_proj(x).view(B, L, 1, self.d_head).expand(-1, -1, self.num_heads, -1)
        V = self.v_proj(x).view(B, L, 1, self.d_head).expand(-1, -1, self.num_heads, -1)
        
        # Attention computation remains the same
        attention = torch.softmax(Q @ K.transpose(-1, -2) / math.sqrt(self.d_head), dim=-1)
        out = attention @ V
        return out.reshape(B, L, D)
```

### Mathematical Difference:
```
Vanilla MHA:  Q_i, K_i, V_i = x W_q^i, x W_k^i, x W_v^i  (for each head i)

MQA:          Q_i = x W_q^i  (separate for each head)
              K, V = x W_k, x W_v  (shared across heads)
```

