## Summary Comparison Table

| Feature | Vanilla Transformer | Modern LLMs | Key Benefits |
|---------|-------------------|-------------|--------------|
| LayerNorm | Pre-norm | Post-norm | Better gradient flow |
| Attention | Multi-head (separate K,V) | MQA/GQA | Memory efficiency |
| KV Storage | Recompute each time | KV Cache | Faster generation |
| FFN | ReLU activation | SwiGLU/GeGLU | Better performance |
| Scaling | Dense computation | MoE | Parameter efficiency |
| Position | Absolute embedding | RoPE | Better extrapolation |
| Memory | O(n²) attention | Flash Attention | Reduced memory |
| KV Compression | Full storage | MLA variants | Smaller cache |

Each of these innovations addresses specific limitations of the vanilla transformer, leading to more efficient, scalable, and capable language models.
